third_party/vsvig/VSViG.py and third_party/vsvig/dy_point_order.pt
  From VSViG, https://github.com/xuyankun/VSViG
  Yankun Xu, Junzhe Wang, Yun-Hsuan Chen, Jie Yang, Wenjie Ming, Shuang Wang and Mohamad Sawan,
  "VSViG: Real-Time Video-Based Seizure Detection via Skeleton-Based Spatiotemporal ViG", ECCV 2024.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (third_party/vsvig/LICENSE).
  Modified: removed timm/torchvision imports; the partition file path is resolved next to VSViG.py.

Models and data used at run time are not included and keep their own licences:
  VSViG-base weights and the WU-SAHZU-EMU-Video dataset (Apache-2.0, by the VSViG authors);
  rtmlib, RTMPose and YOLOX (Apache-2.0); the YOLOX-tiny checkpoint was trained with Human-Art
  (non-commercial licence) and the RTMPose body7/hand5 checkpoints include research-only datasets;
  MCEC_Seizure skeletons (CC BY 4.0, Kuang et al., 2024).
  Optional: MediaPipe and the MediaPipe Face Landmarker model bundle (BlazeFace short-range, Face Mesh V2,
  Blendshape V2), Google, Apache-2.0, https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe. The model cards
  describe AR/entertainment use and state the models are not intended for life-critical decisions;
  see docs/FACE_LANDMARKS.md.

Face de-identification measurements (docs/FACE_SWAP_LICENCES.md, docs/FACE_DEID_TRADEOFF.md) were made on
clips that are not included in this repository:
  GRID audio-visual speech corpus, M. Cooke, J. Barker, S. Cunningham and X. Shao (2006),
  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3625687, CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
  Intel IoT DevKit sample videos, Intel Corporation, https://github.com/intel-iot-devkit/sample-videos,
  CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
Only numbers derived from the clips are included; no frames.
Optional face-check models fetched by scripts/fetch_models.py --face-check, not included: YuNet (OpenCV Zoo,
MIT) and SFace (OpenCV Zoo, Apache-2.0). Optional face-swap backends (src/deid_ghost.py,
src/deid_liveportrait.py) load third-party code and weights from a local location; none of it is included,
and their licences are listed in docs/FACE_SWAP_LICENCES.md.
Outputs of the face-swap backends and their weights stay local and are used for non-commercial research only;
docs/FACE_SWAP_LICENCES.md ("Licence evidence and use") lists each component's licence and what may be published.
